C++ Payment Processing System
Description

This C++ program demonstrates run-time polymorphism using a real-world payment processing system.

The program uses an abstract Payment class as a common interface. Different payment classes such as CardPayment, UpiPayment, and NetBankingPayment provide their own implementation of the pay() function.

Classes Used
1. Payment Class

The Payment class is the abstract base class.

It contains the pure virtual pay() function.
It contains a virtual destructor.
The pay() function defines a common interface for different payment methods.

The pure virtual function is:

virtual void pay(double amount) const = 0;
2. CardPayment Class

The CardPayment class inherits from Payment.

It overrides the pay() function.
It displays the payment amount and "using card".
3. UpiPayment Class

The UpiPayment class inherits from Payment.

It overrides the pay() function.
It displays the payment amount and "using UPI".
4. NetBankingPayment Class

The NetBankingPayment class inherits from Payment.

It overrides the pay() function.
It displays the payment amount and "using net banking".
processPayment() Function

The function:

void processPayment(const Payment& payment, double amount)

accepts a base-class reference.

It calls:

payment.pay(amount);

Because pay() is virtual, the appropriate payment class's implementation is selected at run time.

Main Function

In the main() function, three payment objects are created:

Card Payment → Rs. 1250
UPI Payment → Rs. 750
Net Banking → Rs. 500

Each object is passed to processPayment().

Output
Paid Rs. 1250 using card
Paid Rs. 750 using UPI
Paid Rs. 500 using net banking
OOP Concept Used

Run-Time Polymorphism — Abstract Class and Virtual Function

                  Payment
                     |
             pure virtual pay()
                     |
        +------------+------------+
        |            |            |
      Card          UPI       Net Banking
        |            |            |
     pay()         pay()        pay()
        |            |            |
       Card          UPI      Net Banking

The same processPayment() function can process different payment types through a common Payment interface.